(import :clan/poo/object)
(export DesignReadings)
(def DesignReadings
  (.o inspections: (list
(.o identity: 'compact-observed-who-decides-f00d29a34621 view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "f00d29a346214c3c15d16623f8b5240f39b80167c3955b1f6b1f8623a7b7555c" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the actual PNG and independently displayed standalone SVG. I can start at amber result R, follow the separate copy across its boundary, and reach Scheme on the short direct line. The retained originals and current A/B/C Context feed that same check. Optional work is a side branch returning a proposal, not another authority. The red condition keeps v0; only the green accepted branch adds R and its links to A/B/C. The before and after pictures are local alternatives, so I do not read delivery as guaranteed admission or the illustration as an execution schedule.")
(.o identity: 'compact-observed-what-completes-f00d29a34621 view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "f00d29a346214c3c15d16623f8b5240f39b80167c3955b1f6b1f8623a7b7555c" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The copied result and the live objects are visually distinct, with the live-object caption wrapped clear of the observation branch. I can follow receipt to the Session ledger separately from the owner-key arrow. Arrived is checked while Finished remains empty. The changed Context has its own crossed does-not-finish statement. Thus receiving, admitting and recording a final outcome remain separate decisions in the picture. The branch clears the heading and captions in the actual rendered image.")
(.o identity: 'compact-observed-what-is-open-f00d29a34621 view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "f00d29a346214c3c15d16623f8b5240f39b80167c3955b1f6b1f8623a7b7555c" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "I can point to three brown site-specific qualifications: the full control route is not reserved, the real Context service link is missing, and the memory limit before start is missing. The check also says same Context, same VM and no VM per Session. These short notes remain visible beside the relevant transport or runtime explanation; the picture does not claim deployment qualification. This records what I can trace in this image, without treating coverage as a learner study.")
(.o identity: 'illustrated-fourth-current-state view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "ab7dd7035e1d8d1cef3af1768024271226680c8c476c43597ef220c489894555" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the PNG and the standalone SVG, then checked actual route/text geometry. The copy caption is now clear. Sampling found one remaining contact: the keep-v0 arrow enters the first words of A, B and C are already here. Move its endpoint into the clear gap above the current-state caption, keeping the same conditional return to v0.")
(.o identity: 'illustrated-third-completion view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "f66369348685d113d193ad684dc1c5440b14d52caab618457bb3fc40523ccc7c" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed both the actual PNG and the independently rendered standalone SVG. The observation branch now avoids the Session heading, but its vertical segment touches the left edge of Live objects stay in their VM. Wrap this copy explanation into two short lines to keep its words clear of the observation route. The current Context still has an outstanding copied-boundary explanation request.")
(.o identity: 'illustrated-second-authority view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "855b7f3464a421d779fd4a7077a3e5f87b8ffad674f9eacb50f7b508623092e7" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the revised exported PNG. R now has a short direct route into the check; current and changed Context are close together. One remaining local defect is that the end of check against originals still touches the vertical current-source route. Move that label left into clear space.")
(.o identity: 'illustrated-second-completion view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "855b7f3464a421d779fd4a7077a3e5f87b8ffad674f9eacb50f7b508623092e7" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The independent owner and Session receipt are legible after caption wrapping. The dotted arrival branch still crosses the question heading above the Session, which can be mistaken for an underline or divider. Route that branch around the heading within its local area.")
(.o identity: 'illustrated-second-qualifications view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "855b7f3464a421d779fd4a7077a3e5f87b8ffad674f9eacb50f7b508623092e7" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "The qualification lines are shorter and no longer run into each other, but the right end of the control note is still too close to the dotted observation branch. Move the branch away rather than remove or weaken the qualification.")
(.o identity: 'illustrated-first-authority view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "445fe9f97deed4880997f451e202c3d0c65175601d609970217c9de0265840e6" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "I actually viewed the exported PNG. The main R path is now a local left-to-right line and the two Context possibilities are beside the check. However, the proposal label and the current-sources label are crossed by their own routes, and the introductory sentence touches optional-work artwork. I should move those labels into nearby clear space before treating this as a readable explanation.")
(.o identity: 'illustrated-first-completion view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "445fe9f97deed4880997f451e202c3d0c65175601d609970217c9de0265840e6" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The receipt branch reaches a separate Session ledger and an independent owner key. But the dotted arrival line passes through the control qualification, and the long owner caption is clipped at the left edge. These are physical reading defects in the actual image, even though the declared relations are present.")
(.o identity: 'illustrated-first-qualifications view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "445fe9f97deed4880997f451e202c3d0c65175601d609970217c9de0265840e6" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "The three missing deployment guarantees remain near the affected sites. I can see that the control note runs into the neighboring export note and the observation path. They need shorter lines and separation, not deletion or a favorable review flag.")
(.o identity: 'spatial-who-decides view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "b23560982e30201064b320ffe1eccece5ecd211e714cbc5771851ff2e82f3eae" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "From a novice perspective, the right upper region is mostly unused while both copy-to-check and copy-to-optional-work paths go around the entire picture. I must follow a long perimeter before seeing why R may change Context. The current information, originals, check and before/after views should form a local causal neighborhood, not separate islands connected after placement.")
(.o identity: 'spatial-what-completes view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "b23560982e30201064b320ffe1eccece5ecd211e714cbc5771851ff2e82f3eae" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The copy is visible, but its next destinations are far away across a wrapping boundary. The continuous line is technically connected yet costly to trace. The diagram should keep arrival, copy and the nearby admission explanation spatially coherent, while preserving the independent outcome branch.")
(.o identity: 'spatial-what-is-open view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "b23560982e30201064b320ffe1eccece5ecd211e714cbc5771851ff2e82f3eae" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "The caveats are attached to their sites, but the overall right upper whitespace and long detours reduce the space available to explain the main mechanism. Scientific use of space should preserve visual proximity between reasons, decision and change rather than merely filling a rectangular canvas.")
(.o identity: 'plain-mechanism-who-decides view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "b23560982e30201064b320ffe1eccece5ecd211e714cbc5771851ff2e82f3eae" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "Reading the actual PNG and the exported SVG preview, I start with result R at the upper left, not the owner key. I follow the result-R arrow to a separate copy crossing into the runtime home; the live objects remain inside. The direct-copy path and optional-work path both reach Scheme checks. The original facts/rules/proof and the current Context feed those checks. If R is not accepted I follow the red keep-v0 branch, where A/B/C remain. Only if Scheme accepts R do I follow the green branch to v1, which keeps A/B/C and adds R and its links. These are visible conditional relationships; I do not infer that every arrival is accepted or that the drawing schedules the execution.")
(.o identity: 'plain-mechanism-what-completes view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "b23560982e30201064b320ffe1eccece5ecd211e714cbc5771851ff2e82f3eae" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "From the same arrival I follow the dotted observation-only branch to the Session ledger: Arrived is checked and Finished remains empty. A separate owner-key branch records the final outcome. The changed Context contains a red crossed statement that it does not finish the Session. Thus I can identify what event is merely a receipt, what can change working information, and which independent decision can record an outcome. The visible wording now uses separate copy, live objects and final outcome instead of roots and terminal.")
(.o identity: 'plain-mechanism-what-is-open view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "b23560982e30201064b320ffe1eccece5ecd211e714cbc5771851ff2e82f3eae" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "The annotations qualify the actual sites rather than occupying an isolated row. At incoming R, room for control messages is not reserved along the full route. At the copy boundary, the real Context service link is still missing. At the shared runtime home of the checker, the before-start memory limit is missing; the note also states there is no VM per Session. These remain source-qualified design gaps. This reading records relationships I can point to in the image, not an empirical claim that a child has understood every concept.")
(.o identity: 'ordered-who-decides view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "dd4c897c01e7cddefeae4205ff9c17c1253f10a899c66fd199b9dc61b5eaa023" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "The entry is now result R at upper left. Its copy and optional work paths reach the same checker; originals and the current Context feed that check. The two visible outcomes preserve A/B/C or add R. But the edge wording source/policy cut is unexplained terminology for a first-time learner and should be replaced by ordinary language without changing the source condition.")
(.o identity: 'ordered-what-completes view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "dd4c897c01e7cddefeae4205ff9c17c1253f10a899c66fd199b9dc61b5eaa023" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The same R arrival has an observation-only branch to the Session ledger, separate from the owner decision. The red crossed statement on the changed Context prevents interpreting admission as Session completion. The word terminal on the owner link is unnecessary specialist vocabulary; final outcome expresses the intended distinction more directly. Likewise objects stay is clearer than roots stay for explaining why a copy crosses the boundary.")
(.o identity: 'ordered-what-is-open view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "dd4c897c01e7cddefeae4205ff9c17c1253f10a899c66fd199b9dc61b5eaa023" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "The missing guarantees are attached to their actual sites, but pre-setup heap and end-to-end reserve presume prior runtime vocabulary. Their source references should remain precise while the visible captions explain a before-start memory limit and capacity along the full control-message route.")
(.o identity: 'connected-who-decides view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "31491007747dc16971d0659c68626b2b1616362d7b81f44aab75e13a96f388a2" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "I can follow R from arrival across the owned-copy handoff. Its direct route and the optional calculation route both reach Scheme checks. The originals feed those checks and Context v0 supplies the current source/policy cut. The red not-admitted branch preserves v0; the green admitted branch adds R and its links in v1. However the topmost object is the Session owner, which makes the visual entry point misleading for a novice asked to follow R.")
(.o identity: 'connected-what-completes view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "31491007747dc16971d0659c68626b2b1616362d7b81f44aab75e13a96f388a2" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The copy illustration now agrees with the handoff direction: R crosses into the VM while live roots stay behind. The dashed observation-only link reaches the Session ledger, whose Arrived row is checked and Finished row is empty. A separate owner key has the terminal-decision link. Context v1 has an explicit crossed no-effect statement saying it does not finish the Session, rather than an execution edge that suggests it does.")
(.o identity: 'connected-what-is-open view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "31491007747dc16971d0659c68626b2b1616362d7b81f44aab75e13a96f388a2" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "I can locate each caveat at its affected site: unfinished end-to-end control reserve at arrival, missing production Context export at the byte handoff, and the pre-setup heap limit at the pinned runtime home of the checker. These are attached qualifications, not extra steps before a result can be processed in the already qualified fixture. They do not claim production completion.")
(.o identity: 'long-who-decides view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "d686059da84b60985c5f7282ef7fc16fc4b9196a6750c129eba353ce5669d36e" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "I can now trace the candidate into checks and distinguish Context v0 from the possible v1. But the tall layout leaves large empty areas. The copied-byte picture points outward while the explanatory path sends the candidate inward, which can confuse a novice about what moves.")
(.o identity: 'long-what-completes view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "d686059da84b60985c5f7282ef7fc16fc4b9196a6750c129eba353ce5669d36e" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The arrival-only dashed relation spans almost the entire page. The negative admission-to-completion relation is ranked like a possible execution step, adding layout depth even though it has no propagating effect. These distinctions need a clear no-effect mark and a compact independent Session branch.")
(.o identity: 'long-what-is-open view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "d686059da84b60985c5f7282ef7fc16fc4b9196a6750c129eba353ce5669d36e" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "The qualifications are now attached to the sites they qualify. However the long presentation still demands scrolling between the incoming result and its consequences. A more compact overall arrangement is needed to explain the same mechanism with lower visual tracking cost.")
(.o identity: 'too-wide-who-decides view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "36780bb44a613f43bef811d24b853b716268adb84ee31ca139011990149dad8a" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "The actual connected picture is compressed into a very wide strip. Measured text is about 7px; the student cannot read the relation labels or follow the conditions. Separate qualification nodes add routing depth and empty space. The existence of edges does not make this explanation readable.")
(.o identity: 'too-wide-what-completes view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "36780bb44a613f43bef811d24b853b716268adb84ee31ca139011990149dad8a" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The actual connected picture is compressed into a very wide strip. Measured text is about 7px; the student cannot read the relation labels or follow the conditions. Separate qualification nodes add routing depth and empty space. The existence of edges does not make this explanation readable.")
(.o identity: 'too-wide-what-is-open view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "36780bb44a613f43bef811d24b853b716268adb84ee31ca139011990149dad8a" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "The actual connected picture is compressed into a very wide strip. Measured text is about 7px; the student cannot read the relation labels or follow the conditions. Separate qualification nodes add routing depth and empty space. The existence of edges does not make this explanation readable.")
(.o identity: 'reconsider-who-decides view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "6c2414178122f076875df0ccd9daba986ca23f90d8dcef54917217d549073ba7" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "A novice can identify the separate pictures, but cannot follow candidate R from its arrival to any check or to an actual before/after Context state. The admitted and unchanged consequences are not linked to the same Context object.")
(.o identity: 'reconsider-what-completes view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "6c2414178122f076875df0ccd9daba986ca23f90d8dcef54917217d549073ba7" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The ledger illustration is isolated from both arrival and Context admission. The viewer must invent why those events cannot finish the task and where a final outcome would come from.")
(.o identity: 'reconsider-what-is-open view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "6c2414178122f076875df0ccd9daba986ca23f90d8dcef54917217d549073ba7" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "Three gap pictures occupy their own row. They do not qualify the actual ingress, copy boundary or VM home in a connected mechanism. Matching labels and request counts cannot show a student understood those causal constraints.")
(.o identity: 'vector-who-decides view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "6c2414178122f076875df0ccd9daba986ca23f90d8dcef54917217d549073ba7" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "I inspected the new PNG and the exported SVG preview. The same message is shown before and after arrival, without gaining a fact-approval mark. The source/permission/rule gate has a conditional admission branch and a separate no-change branch; SOURCE is now fully visible below the moved lens. Two A requests converge on VM A, B has its own home, and the calculator returns an amber question-mark proposal rather than an admitted fact. The captions are adjacent to their objects with no observed collisions. The first question is answered by these contrasts rather than native containment frames.")
(.o identity: 'vector-what-completes view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "6c2414178122f076875df0ccd9daba986ca23f90d8dcef54917217d549073ba7" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The small detached blue page starts inside the VM and its copies cross the dashed boundary; the live-root network stays behind. The separate result page points to retained FACTS, RULES and PROOF books. The Session ledger has Arrived checked and Finished empty, with a separate owner-decision indication. These pictures distinguish transport, source retention and terminal authority. I rechecked the SVG preview: the same objects and question grouping are retained, not rasterized into an image wrapper.")
(.o identity: 'vector-what-is-open view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "6c2414178122f076875df0ccd9daba986ca23f90d8dcef54917217d549073ba7" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "The data lane is continuous while the control route has a visible break, matching the unfinished end-to-end reserve qualification. The host plug is disconnected from the Context socket and the caption scopes the gap to production export. The memory drawing has a missing limit line before the start switch, with a not-implemented caption. All three are depicted as outstanding boundaries, rather than completed protection. The exported SVG now retains the three question bands as vector shapes.")
(.o identity: 'separated-who-decides view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "d6a652b7751115fcd565a55e509dc59c38fde4180eb2a9ca4ac5af652b1b89af" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "The corrected viewport separates the arrival tray, conditional admission/no-change branch, pinned A/B homes and calculator proposal from their captions. However the magnifying lens still covers part of SOURCE inside the check gate. That is a remaining depiction defect, not a successful explanation of every check.")
(.o identity: 'separated-what-completes view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "d6a652b7751115fcd565a55e509dc59c38fde4180eb2a9ca4ac5af652b1b89af" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The detached blue page, rather than the live-root network, now crosses the dashed boundary. The source books stay put and a separate page points back to them. In the Session ledger, Arrived is checked while Finished is empty. The captions and object labels no longer collide; these visible differences explain why copying, source retention and a final outcome are separate.")
(.o identity: 'separated-what-is-open view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "d6a652b7751115fcd565a55e509dc59c38fde4180eb2a9ca4ac5af652b1b89af" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "The complete data lane contrasts with a broken control lane. The service plug does not reach the Context socket. A missing limit line precedes the start symbol. Each picture has a separate explicit not-implemented qualification, so none of the three is depicted as a completed deployment feature.")
(.o identity: 'grid-who-decides view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "862a6f941183cd2c51537f1727189bc781a25dcc99008e0492b3135db4641c7c" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "The same envelope reaches a tray without an authority change; candidate checks visibly branch into admission or no change, repeated A requests share VM A, and the calculator returns a question-mark proposal. However RECEIVED, VM labels and proposal labels collide with the explanatory titles. These collisions make the relationships hard to read.")
(.o identity: 'grid-what-completes view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "862a6f941183cd2c51537f1727189bc781a25dcc99008e0492b3135db4641c7c" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The copy crosses a dashed VM boundary while live roots stay inside. A result references retained fact/rule/proof books. The Session ledger marks Arrived but leaves Finished empty. These are useful visible distinctions, but roots stay, the book lettering and separate owner decision overlap the main captions.")
(.o identity: 'grid-what-is-open view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "862a6f941183cd2c51537f1727189bc781a25dcc99008e0492b3135db4641c7c" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "A broken control route, disconnected service plug and absent pre-start memory limit give three different reasons for the implementation gaps. Their explanatory labels overlap the main titles, so this layout is not usable despite legible individual text sizes.")
(.o identity: 'novice-mechanism view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "f4fdec7d538c50e1997f4862b011404ff342f8639b90d7877263ee673185367a" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "The actual image lists technical roles inside nested frames. It does not show an arriving item changing state through inspection. Understanding who decides still depends on reading I/O, Context and VM captions. Replacing these symbols with child characters would not make the missing mechanism visible.")
(.o identity: 'novice-completion view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "f4fdec7d538c50e1997f4862b011404ff342f8639b90d7877263ee673185367a" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "Original evidence and independent Sessions sit side by side with no visible relation to the proposed result. The viewer must infer the difference between arrival, admission and completion from technical sentences; the pictures do not explain that distinction.")
(.o identity: 'novice-space view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "f4fdec7d538c50e1997f4862b011404ff342f8639b90d7877263ee673185367a" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "A large empty region beneath optional CPU work and repeated enclosure margins separate the few visible symbols. The implementation caveats are readable but presented as vocabulary-heavy lines rather than visible contrasts. Typography alone does not establish novice comprehension.")
(.o identity: 'simple-owner view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "ddb8380549c7d17274f2c0eff0dbc56878baffe6cc12af917c3693599a35c1c9" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "The optional VM frame is gone and the principal roles remain readable at 20px. The owner heading still says fixed owner without stating what must stay on it; a beginner could confuse a Context domain with a Session. The same-domain/same-owner rule needs an explicit explanation.")
(.o identity: 'simple-terminal view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "ddb8380549c7d17274f2c0eff0dbc56878baffe6cc12af917c3693599a35c1c9" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "Copied bytes are distinguished from VM roots; the originals remain outside result production, and independent Sessions own final outcomes. The endpoint caption explicitly denies that I/O completion can finish a Session.")
(.o identity: 'simple-gap view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda image-sha: "ddb8380549c7d17274f2c0eff0dbc56878baffe6cc12af917c3693599a35c1c9" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "The broken amber lane now matches the not-end-to-end caption rather than promising protection. Context export and the heap limit before setup remain explicitly not implemented.")

(.o identity: 'packed-owner view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda
 image-sha: "107cbcf53ec64d5c70594113ba135cd2a5f53c3f44d36511051ed7f5c91db64e" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "I can read that Tokio reports arrivals and cannot admit Context results; Scheme owns decisions and optional CPU work only proposes. The owner and one-child VM enclosures duplicate the locality explanation and consume a large vertical block. A simpler projected boundary would reduce the reading burden without moving the native objects.")
(.o identity: 'packed-terminal view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda
 image-sha: "107cbcf53ec64d5c70594113ba135cd2a5f53c3f44d36511051ed7f5c91db64e" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The copied-byte boundary keeps VM roots local. Original facts, rules and proof inputs remain separate from returned results. Independent Sessions own attempts and final outcomes, and the caption explicitly says I/O cannot finish a Session.")
(.o identity: 'packed-gap view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda
 image-sha: "107cbcf53ec64d5c70594113ba135cd2a5f53c3f44d36511051ed7f5c91db64e" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "All three outstanding implementation qualifications are readable. However the complete shield on the control lane visually suggests end-to-end protection even though the adjacent caption says it is not end-to-end yet.")

    (.o identity: 'wide-owners view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda
        image-sha: "e487fb2cd8c648adf660bddafe51732eaeddbabd8ce5c0b880bfe7662715a8bc" question: 'who-decides producer: 'current-model response: "The actual 1600px image compresses leaf text to about 7px. Large nested owner frames occupy a single horizontal strip; the novice cannot reliably follow I/O versus semantic ownership.")
    (.o identity: 'wide-terminal view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda
        image-sha: "e487fb2cd8c648adf660bddafe51732eaeddbabd8ce5c0b880bfe7662715a8bc" question: 'what-completes producer: 'current-model response: "The archive and endpoint glyphs are present, but the completion and original-evidence qualifications are too small to read at the delivered scale. I cannot treat those tiny captions as a usable answer.")
    (.o identity: 'wide-gaps view: 'hybrid-allocation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-29a617ccdea461d56209db94908d0af6a222527fc7e03cb2b53ea058907b6dda
        image-sha: "e487fb2cd8c648adf660bddafe51732eaeddbabd8ce5c0b880bfe7662715a8bc" question: 'what-is-open producer: 'current-model response: "The pending boundaries are colored, yet their implementation qualifications are too small. The image does not let the learner distinguish proposed boundaries from completed ones with low reading effort.")
